  "graphql-federation-practice/README.md": {
    "lang": "text",
    "lines": 87,
    "content": "# GraphQL Federation Resolver & Microservice Integration\n\n## Overview\n\nTechFlow Inc. operates a distributed microservices architecture with a GraphQL Supergraph (Apollo Federation) serving as the unified API gateway. You will implement a GraphQL subgraph resolver in Node.js and a backend microservice in Java/Spring Boot.\n\n## File Structure\n\n```text\n.\n├── node-subgraph/\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── resolvers/orderResolvers.js       (EDIT THIS)\n│   │   ├── dataSources/orderDataSource.js    (PROVIDED)\n│   │   ├── schema.graphql                     (PROVIDED)\n│   │   └── index.js                           (PROVIDED)\n│   ├── package.json                           (PROVIDED)\n│   └── __tests__/resolvers.test.js            (PROVIDED)\n├── java-service/\n│   ├── src/main/java/com/techflow/orders/\n│   │   ├── controller/OrderController.java    (EDIT THIS)\n│   │   ├── service/OrderService.java          (PROVIDED)\n│   │   ├── exception/                         (PROVIDED)\n│   │   ├── config/                            (PROVIDED)\n│   │   ├── dto/                               (PROVIDED)\n│   │   ├── model/                             (PROVIDED)\n│   │   └── repository/                        (PROVIDED)\n│   ├── src/test/java/com/techflow/orders/OrderControllerTest.java\n│   └── pom.xml\n└── QUESTIONS.md                               (EDIT THIS)\n```\n\n## How to Run and Test\n\n### Node.js GraphQL Subgraph\n\n```bash\ncd node-subgraph\nnpm install\nnpm start\n```\n\n```bash\nnpm test\n```\n\n### Java Spring Boot Service\n\n```bash\ncd java-service\nmvn spring-boot:run\n```\n\n```bash\nmvn test\n```\n\nThe tests are provided to help validate incremental progress.\n\n# [REQUIRED] Your Tasks\n\n## Task 1: GraphQL Subgraph Resolver with Federation\n\nImplement resolver logic in `node-subgraph/src/resolvers/orderResolvers.js`:\n\n- Implement `User.orders` with proper error handling\n- Implement `Order.shippingInfo` using the provided DataLoader\n- Implement `Query.orders` to fetch orders by user ID\n\nThe starter code also contains related TODOs and integration issues that may need attention.\n\n## Task 2: Spring Boot REST Controller\n\nImplement REST endpoints in `java-service/src/main/java/com/techflow/orders/controller/OrderController.java`:\n\n- `GET /api/orders`\n- `GET /api/orders/{id}`\n- `GET /api/orders/user/{userId}`\n- `POST /api/orders`\n- `PATCH /api/orders/{id}/status`\n- `DELETE /api/orders/{id}`\n\nUse the provided `OrderService` for business logic.\n\n## Written Questions\n\nAnswer the questions in `QUESTIONS.md`."
  },
